## 1. The Pitch {#1-the-pitch}

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Memorize this.** Every teammate should be able to deliver this in 30 seconds.

**Sentinel NER** is an **operational landslide intelligence and intervention platform** for Northeast India. It doesn't just *predict* landslides — it converts hazard intelligence into **accountable, time-bound operational decisions** for people, infrastructure, and emergency agencies.

### The Magic Formula:
```
Detect → Predict → Understand Consequences → Decide → Act → Verify → Learn
```

### One-Line Differentiator:
> *"Existing systems can tell you a landslide might happen. Sentinel NER tells you **which road chainage** is at risk, **which villages** could become isolated, **who** needs to act, **what** they should do, and **by when** — then tracks whether they actually did it."*

---

## 2. Why This Problem Matters {#2-problem-context}

### The Operational Gap (This is what SIH judges care about)

India has:
- **GSI/NLFC**: National Landslide Forecast Centre — provides susceptibility maps
- **IMD**: India Meteorological Department — provides rainfall forecasts
- **ISRO/NRSC**: Indian Space Research Organisation — provides satellite imagery
- **NDMA**: National Disaster Management Authority — provides guidelines

> [!CAUTION]
> **The gap is NOT in detection. The gap is in OPERATIONS.**

Currently, when IMD says "heavy rainfall expected" and GSI says "this area is susceptible":
- ❌ Nobody knows which **specific slope** is most dangerous right now
- ❌ Nobody knows which **road chainage (kilometer marker)** will be blocked
- ❌ Nobody knows which **villages will become isolated** if that road is cut
- ❌ Nobody knows **who exactly** should inspect, close, or reroute
- ❌ Nobody tracks whether the recommended action was **actually done**
- ❌ There's no **audit trail** linking prediction → action → outcome

**Sentinel NER fills this entire chain.**

### Target Region: Northeast India
- **Primary corridors**: Mizoram (NH-54, NH-306), Assam, Sikkim, Meghalaya, Arunachal Pradesh
- **Why NER?**: Highest landslide density in India, fragile terrain, limited road connectivity, single-road-dependency for entire districts
- **Real impact**: When NH-54 between Aizawl and Lunglei is blocked, 500,000+ people lose their only supply route

---

## 3. The Core Innovation {#3-core-innovation}

> [!TIP]
> **What makes this different from every other "landslide prediction system"** — this is what wins competitions.

### 3.1 We Are NOT Claiming:
Read the [PRD Section 14](file:///c:/Users/Abhishek/SIH%20-%202026/.prd/ner_prd) — **Competitive/Novelty Guardrails**:

We do NOT claim uniqueness for:
- Rainfall thresholds (every system does this)
- Susceptibility mapping (GSI already does this)
- IoT sensors (many projects claim this)
- Satellite monitoring (ISRO already does this)
- Generic ML prediction (hundreds of papers exist)
- Generic evacuation routing (Google Maps does this)

### 3.2 What We ARE Claiming:
Our differentiation is the **integrated operational chain**:

```mermaid
graph LR
    A[Environmental Change] --> B[Slope-Level Risk]
    B --> C[Road & Asset Consequence]
    C --> D[Responsible Actor]
    D --> E[Time-Bound Deadline]
    E --> F[Authorized Action]
    F --> G[Verified Outcome]
    G --> H[Audit & Learning]
```

Plus these NER-specific innovations:
1. **Lifeline Graph Analysis**: Roads as a network graph — when one edge fails, calculate isolation impact
2. **Forecast vs. Interception Mode**: Different operational profiles for slow-onset (days of warning) vs. rapid (hours/minutes) events
3. **Degraded Connectivity Operations**: The system works even when network is down (offline field app)
4. **Strict Non-Autonomous Boundary**: AI recommends; authorized humans approve — this is *by design*, not a limitation
5. **Warning Ledger**: Cryptographic, append-only audit trail of every prediction → action → outcome

---

## 4. Architecture Overview — The 10-Stage Pipeline {#4-architecture}

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Every teammate must understand this pipeline.** Judges will walk you through it.

```mermaid
graph TB
    S1[Stage 1: Foundation<br/>FastAPI + Next.js + CI/CD] --> S2[Stage 2: Security & RBAC<br/>JWT, Roles, Audit]
    S2 --> S3[Stage 3: Domain Data & Geospatial<br/>Districts, Slopes, Roads, Villages, Assets]
    S3 --> S4[Stage 4: Operational Map<br/>Leaflet, Layers, Spatial Queries]
    S4 --> S5[Stage 5: Risk Engine<br/>Transparent ML, Calibration, Provenance]
    S5 --> S6[Stage 6: Satellite & InSAR<br/>Change Detection, Deformation]
    S6 --> S7[Stage 7: Consequence Engine<br/>Road/Asset/Village Impact Graph]
    S7 --> S8[Stage 8: Operational Control<br/>Actions, Warnings, Ledger]
    S8 --> S9[Stage 9: Alerts & Connectivity<br/>Multi-Channel Delivery, Offline Mode]
    S9 --> S10[Stage 10: Community Intelligence<br/>Citizen Reports, Field Sensors]
```

### Why Stages Matter:
Each stage builds on the previous one. This is a **disciplined engineering approach**, not a hackathon mess. Judges love seeing:
- Clear separation of concerns
- Each stage independently testable
- Stage-gate verification scripts for every stage

