## 6. Tech Stack Breakdown {#6-tech-stack}

### Backend

| Technology | Purpose | Why This Choice |
|-----------|---------|----------------|
| **Python 3.11+** | Backend language | Geospatial ecosystem (Shapely, GeoPandas), ML ecosystem |
| **FastAPI** | Web framework | Async, automatic OpenAPI docs, Pydantic integration |
| **Pydantic v2** | Data validation | Type-safe schemas, serialization, config management |
| **MongoDB Atlas** | Primary database | GeoJSON native support, `2dsphere` indexes, flexible schema |
| **Redis** | Caching & rate limiting | Fast in-memory store |
| **Celery** | Background tasks | Async processing for satellite/risk pipelines |
| **JWT (PyJWT)** | Authentication | Stateless tokens, role embedding |

### Frontend

| Technology | Purpose | Why This Choice |
|-----------|---------|----------------|
| **Next.js (App Router)** | Framework | SSR, file-based routing, TypeScript-first |
| **React 18** | UI library | Component model, concurrent features |
| **TypeScript** | Language | Type safety across API contracts |
| **Tailwind CSS** | Styling | Utility-first, responsive, dark mode |
| **Leaflet** | Map engine | Open source, zero API keys, lightweight |
| **TanStack Query** | Data fetching | Caching, background refetch, optimistic updates |
| **Zustand** | State management | Minimal, TypeScript-friendly |
| **Lucide React** | Icons | Consistent, accessible SVG icons |

### Infrastructure

| Technology | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|
| **Docker** | Containerization |
| **GitHub Actions** | CI/CD pipeline |
| **AWS S3** | Object storage (satellite data) |
| **MongoDB Atlas** | Managed database |

